+/* =============================================================================
+   Options snapshot (informational; the adapter parses the environment once,
+   see interface_hip/ozaki2.cpp for the authoritative implementation).
+   Size-gate defaults were tuned 2026-07-02 on gfx1200 (RX 9060 XT, 16 GiB);
+   re-tune on hardware with stronger fp64.
+
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2                (0/1, default 0: enable routing globally,
+                                  i.e. even outside an _ozaki2 driver scope)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_ALGO           (auto|1stage|2stage, default auto; algorithm
+                                  choice of the _ozaki2 eigensolver drivers,
+                                  see the driver prototypes below)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_NUM_MODULI     (default 15, clamped to 2..20; below 15 the
+                                  routed eigensolvers lose eigenvalue accuracy)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_FASTMODE       (0/1, default 0)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_MIN_DIM        (min(m,n,keff) routing gate on the gemm-
+                                  equivalent dims; real default 128.  Setting
+                                  the base var applies to BOTH dtypes unless
+                                  the _CPLX var is also set)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_MIN_DIM_CPLX   (complex min_dim, default 64)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_MIN_K          (keff = gemm-equivalent inner-dimension gate;
+                                  real default 256)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_MIN_K_CPLX     (complex min_k, default 128)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_MIN_MNK        (m*n*keff product gate; real default 2^28 =
+                                  268435456)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_MIN_MNK_CPLX   (complex min_mnk, default 2^27 = 134217728)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_TRMM_MNK_MULT  (min_mnk multiplier for trmm, default 4:
+                                  its Ozaki path pays an extra out-of-place
+                                  temp + copy-back)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_MAX_WS_MB      (workspace cap in MiB, absolute per process)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_MAX_WS_PERCENT (workspace cap as percent of device VRAM,
+                                  divided by the local rank count below;
+                                  default 30 when MAX_WS_MB is unset; if both
+                                  are set the smaller cap wins)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_MIN_FREE_MB    (default 2048: refuse to grow the workspace
+                                  unless at least this much VRAM stays free
+                                  afterwards — headroom for MAGMA's own
+                                  device allocations, which fail hard while
+                                  our denial is a graceful native fallback)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_LOCAL_RANKS    (processes sharing this GPU; divides the
+                                  percent-based workspace cap.  Default:
+                                  OMPI_COMM_WORLD_LOCAL_SIZE, then
+                                  SLURM_NTASKS_PER_NODE, then 1)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_OPS            (csv subset of gemm,symm,hemm,syr2k,her2k,trmm;
+                                  default all)
+     MAGMA_OZAKI2_VERBOSE        (0/1/2, default 0; 1 = config + atexit stats,
+                                  2 = additionally per-call lines on stderr)
